# ALSA's library keeps its parsed configuration for the process's life;
# a test that opens a device on a machine with ALSA reports it as leaked
# (D401). Nothing of ours is in these frames. Maul Audio loads the library
# at run time and unloads it, so its frames are often unnamed by the time
# LeakSanitizer reports; the calls into it are named by Maul Audio's own
# ALSA files instead (D403).
leak:libasound
leak:maul-audio/src/alsa_
